## What to deliver

Author the muzzle-flash system operation by operation — the stuttering flash core,
the forward spark spit, and the faint smoke wisp, with the forces and per-particle
curves that make them project forward and fade as the brief describes, and the
timeline set to **loop** — running `particle-3d render` to simulate and check the
effect as you go. When the simulated `effect.gif` reads as a continuous small-arms
muzzle flash, run `render` one last time and stop: the recorded `actions.json` (and
the `system.json` it emits) is your finished submission.
